diff --git a/resources/language/resource.language.en_gb/strings.po b/resources/language/resource.language.en_gb/strings.po
index 3c1e841..41952c4 100644
--- a/resources/language/resource.language.en_gb/strings.po
+++ b/resources/language/resource.language.en_gb/strings.po
@@ -1167,3 +1167,67 @@ msgstr ""
 msgctxt "#32920"
 msgid "The time zone could not be detected"
 msgstr ""
+
+msgctxt "#32921"
+msgid "Internal disks"
+msgstr ""
+
+msgctxt "#32922"
+msgid "Show the internal disks (read-only)"
+msgstr ""
+
+msgctxt "#32923"
+msgid "Off (the default): run from a USB drive, this system does not see the disks inside the computer; installed on one of them, it does not see the other disks and does not mount the rest of its own. On: from the next start they are all mounted read-only, and the kernel runs without its lockdown. This makes the entry of the boot menu that shows the internal disks the one that starts by itself; choosing \"run\" in that menu once turns it off again."
+msgstr ""
+
+msgctxt "#32924"
+msgid "With this setting on, from the next start:[CR][CR]- This system sees the disks inside the computer and mounts them read-only: all of them when it runs from a USB drive; when it is installed on one of them, the other disks and the other partitions of its own disk. That is where Windows and your files are.[CR][CR]- Everything that runs here can read them: Kodi and every add-on, also the ones made by other people. With file sharing (Samba) turned on, they can be shared on your network too.[CR][CR]- \"Read-only\" is how the disks are mounted, not a lock. Add-ons run with full rights: one that wanted to could mount them again for writing.[CR][CR]- The kernel runs without its lockdown. In the normal start it loads only the drivers that came with this system and keeps programs away from the memory and the hardware of the computer. In this one it does neither.[CR][CR]- It is so on every computer that this drive is started on.[CR][CR]It stays on until you turn it off here, reset this system to its defaults, or choose \"run\" once in the menu that is shown when the computer starts (on a UEFI computer that entry is \"Run\", not the one that names the internal disks). An update made with the installer for Windows turns it off as well."
+msgstr ""
+
+msgctxt "#32925"
+msgid "Show the internal disks, read-only, to this system and its add-ons from the next start?"
+msgstr ""
+
+msgctxt "#32926"
+msgid "The internal disks will be shown from the next start"
+msgstr ""
+
+msgctxt "#32927"
+msgid "The internal disks will be hidden from the next start"
+msgstr ""
+
+msgctxt "#32928"
+msgid "The boot menu could not be changed, so this was not turned on. Try again; if it keeps failing, restart the system first."
+msgstr ""
+
+msgctxt "#32929"
+msgid "The boot menu could not be changed as asked. The internal disks may still be shown at the next start. To hide them, choose \"run\" in the menu that is shown when the computer starts."
+msgstr ""
+
+msgctxt "#32930"
+msgid "This cannot be changed here: the boot menu of this system is not one that this setting knows (it was changed by hand, or the system was installed in another way), so it is left as it is. If the internal disks are being shown, choose \"run\" in the menu that is shown when the computer starts; if that does not hide them, the boot menu has to be put right by hand."
+msgstr ""
+
+msgctxt "#32931"
+msgid "There is nothing to change: as it is installed, this system does not hide the internal disks. They are shown already."
+msgstr ""
+
+msgctxt "#32932"
+msgid "This cannot be turned on in live mode, which has no way of starting that shows the internal disks. Start by \"run\" first."
+msgstr ""
+
+msgctxt "#32933"
+msgid "The boot partition could not be made read-only again. Restart the system now."
+msgstr ""
+
+msgctxt "#32934"
+msgid "This cannot be changed here: the boot menu of this system could not be found or read. Nothing was changed."
+msgstr ""
+
+msgctxt "#32935"
+msgid "The setting that shows the internal disks could not be turned off, so after the reset they would still be shown. To hide them then, choose \"run\" in the menu that is shown when the computer starts. Go on with the reset?"
+msgstr ""
+
+msgctxt "#32936"
+msgid "Changing the boot menu..."
+msgstr ""
